Backport of upstream Manifold commit 362a2de, "Make LevelSet output independent of thread
scheduling" (elalish/manifold#1848, Robert Kossessa, 2026-09-24), to 7c86359.

The change below is upstream's own, unaltered: it cherry-picks onto 7c86359 cleanly, and this
diff is that result taken relative to 7c86359, so `git apply` takes it as-is there. Applied by the
GeometryEngine authors, 2026-10-22, to the Manifold sources the shipped manifold.dll is built from
(Apache License 2.0, section 4(b): the redistributed binary is built from modified 7c86359).

What it does: Manifold::LevelSet's parallel passes hand out vertex numbers with AtomicAdd and
append triangles in whatever order their threads run, and the halfedge build, topology cleanup
and sorting after them depend on that order, so the same field meshed twice could come back with
different geometry. Each vertex is keyed by where it was made - its grid point and the edge (0-6)
or the grid point itself (7) - and once the triangles are built, vertices are renumbered in key
order and triangles rotated (keeping their winding) and sorted. The sequential and parallel
meshers then give the same mesh, on every call. It also adds upstream's SDF.Determinism test.

Apply from a Manifold checkout at 7c86359:  git apply <this file>

